"text":"Effect on Social Security Benefits\n \n11 - 12","tree_line_end":426,"tree_line_start":408},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Effect on Social Security Benefits\n ","tree_line_end":418,"tree_line_start":410},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Effect on Social Security Benefits\n ","tree_line_end":418,"tree_line_start":414},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"11 - 12","tree_line_end":426,"tree_line_start":419},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"11 - 12","tree_line_end":426,"tree_line_start":423},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"Contacts\n ","tree_line_end":444,"tree_line_start":427},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Contacts","tree_line_end":436,"tree_line_start":429},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Contacts","tree_line_end":436,"tree_line_start":433},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":" ","tree_line_end":444,"tree_line_start":437},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":444,"tree_line_start":441},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":447,"tree_line_start":445},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"INTRODUCTION","tree_line_end":452,"tree_line_start":448},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. This memo provides guidance on the Social Security (Additional Payments) Act 2022\n1\n. The Act came \ninto force on 28.6.22 and extends to England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland.\n \n ","tree_line_end":463,"tree_line_start":453},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP) Act 22","tree_line_end":471,"tree_line_start":464},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"BACKGROUND\n ","tree_line_end":477,"tree_line_start":472},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. The governments cost of living package has confirmed that certain households will receive an \nadditional cost of living payment of up to £650. The payments are part of a package which supports \nvulnerable households helping with the cost of living which were announced by the chancellor in May \n2022. The additional payments will be automatically issued to eligible persons in two separate payments. \nThese additional payments are not taxable and will not affect a person’s benefits or tax credits.\n ","tree_line_end":486,"tree_line_start":478},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 1:\n DWP is using a computer program to identify eligible persons for the additional\n \npayments. \nTherefore, there is no claims process for persons to follow\n \nto claim the additional payments. The \npayments will be paid into the bank\n \n account where claimants normally receive benefits or by the \nclaimant’s preferred\n \nalternative arrangements where applicable.","tree_line_end":503,"tree_line_start":487},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 2:\n This memo provides guidance on the effect of additional payments on\n \nSocial Security Benefits. \nFor guidance on the effect of additional payments on\n \ntax and tax credits contact HMRC.\n ","tree_line_end":515,"tree_line_start":504},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"MEANS-TESTED ADDITIONAL PAYMENTS","tree_line_end":520,"tree_line_start":516},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. A single payment of\n \n ","tree_line_end":526,"tree_line_start":521},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n. £326 to any person who has a qualifying entitlement to a means tested social security benefit payable \nin\n \nrespect of the first qualifying day \nand","tree_line_end":537,"tree_line_start":527},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n £324 to any person who has a qualifying entitlement to a means tested social security benefit payable \nin\n \nrespect of the second qualifying day\n1\n.","tree_line_end":550,"tree_line_start":538},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 1:\n Reference to a “person” is to an individual or to a couple but not to each member of a couple \nseparately.","tree_line_end":557,"tree_line_start":551},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 2:\n \nFor the list of means tested benefits see paragraph 4. For the meaning of qualifying day see \nparagraph 5 and for guidance on qualifying entitlement see paragraph 6.","tree_line_end":565,"tree_line_start":558},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 3:\n Payments will be staggered. The first payment should have been paid into the eligible persons’ \nbank accounts or by their approved alternative method of payment from 14.7.22. It is expected the \nmajority of the first payments will be made by the end of July 2022.\n ","tree_line_end":574,"tree_line_start":566},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP) Act 22, s 1","tree_line_end":580,"tree_line_start":575},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Means tested benefits\n ","tree_line_end":586,"tree_line_start":581},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n \n \n \n \n \nMeans-tested benefits are\n ","tree_line_end":597,"tree_line_start":587},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \nUniversal Credit (UC)","tree_line_end":605,"tree_line_start":598},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n Income-based Jobseeker’s Allowance (JSA(IB))","tree_line_end":612,"tree_line_start":606},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n Income-related Employment and Support Allowance (ESA(IR))","tree_line_end":619,"tree_line_start":613},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4. \nIncome Support (IS)","tree_line_end":626,"tree_line_start":620},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5.\n State Pension Credit (SPC)\n1\n.","tree_line_end":637,"tree_line_start":627},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 1\n:\n \n For the purposes of these additional payments, contributory benefits\n \nare not qualifying benefits.","tree_line_end":647,"tree_line_start":638},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 2\n: Tax credits are also qualifying benefits for the additional payment. For\n \nguidance on the effect \nof\n \nadditional payments on tax and tax credits contact\n \nHMRC.\n ","tree_line_end":660,"tree_line_start":648},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP) Act 22, s 1(3)","tree_line_end":666,"tree_line_start":661},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":670,"tree_line_start":667},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Qualifying day\n ","tree_line_end":676,"tree_line_start":671},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5.\n \n \n \nThe\n ","tree_line_end":685,"tree_line_start":677},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \nqualifying day for the first payment is 25.5.22\n1\n which means the claimant is entitled to a \npayment\n \nof\n ","tree_line_end":700,"tree_line_start":686},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.1\n \nUC in an assessment period ending between 26.4.22 to 25.5.22 \nor","tree_line_end":710,"tree_line_start":701},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.2\n \nJSA(IB), ESA(IR), SPC or IS in the period 26.4.22 to 25.5.22\n \n \nand\n ","tree_line_end":723,"tree_line_start":711},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \nthe\n \nqualifying day for the second payment will be no later than 31.10.22, to be specified by \nthe\n \nSecretary of State in regulations\n2\n.","tree_line_end":739,"tree_line_start":724},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP) Act 22 s 1(1)(a); 2 s 1(4)","tree_line_end":745,"tree_line_start":740},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":749,"tree_line_start":746},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Qualifying entitlements","tree_line_end":754,"tree_line_start":750},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"6.\n \n \n \nA person has a qualifying entitlement to a social security benefit in respect of a qualifying day if in \nrespect of\n ","tree_line_end":764,"tree_line_start":755},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \nUC, the person is entitled to a payment of at least 1p in respect of an assessment period ending \nduring the\n \nperiod of one month ending with the\n \nqualifying day \nor","tree_line_end":779,"tree_line_start":765},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \nSPC, JSA(IB), ESA(IR) or IS, the person is entitled to a payment of at least 1p in respect of any day \nduring\n \nthe period of one month ending with the\n \nqualifying day\n1\n.","tree_line_end":796,"tree_line_start":780},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 1.\n \nFor the meaning of qualifying day see paragraph 5.\n ","tree_line_end":804,"tree_line_start":797},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 2:\n \nA person receiving a payment or having an award does not include payments received or awards \nmade as a result of fraud.","tree_line_end":812,"tree_line_start":805},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 3:\n \nWhere a person has entitlement to UC and another social security benefit on the qualifying day \nsee further guidance at paragraph 7.\n ","tree_line_end":821,"tree_line_start":813},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP) Act 22, s 2","tree_line_end":827,"tree_line_start":822},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Applicable benefits\n ","tree_line_end":832,"tree_line_start":828},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"7.\n \n \n \n Where a person has a qualifying entitlement in respect of a qualifying day to","tree_line_end":840,"tree_line_start":833},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \nUC \nand\n ","tree_line_end":851,"tree_line_start":841},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \nanother social security benefit\n ","tree_line_end":860,"tree_line_start":852},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"the benefit by reference to which the additional cost of living payment in respect of\n \nthe qualifying \nday is to be made is UC\n1\n.","tree_line_end":872,"tree_line_start":861},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS(AP)Act 22, s 3\n ","tree_line_end":879,"tree_line_start":873},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"8.\n \n Where HMRC make a payment to a claimant thinking they are someone who does not have \nentitlement to a DWP benefit and it later transpires that the claimant does have an entitlement to a DWP \nbenefit in the qualifying period, the original HMRC payment is treated as if it were the correctly made \npayment by DWP\n1\n.\n ","tree_line_end":893,"tree_line_start":880},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS(AP)Act 22 s 6 & 7(5)","tree_line_end":899,"tree_line_start":894},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":903,"tree_line_start":900},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"DISABILITY ADDITIONAL PAYMENTS","tree_line_end":908,"tree_line_start":904},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"9. The Secretary of State will issue a further disability additional single payment of £150 to anyone who is \nentitled to a payment of a disability benefit that is payable in respect of 25.5.22\n1\n.","tree_line_end":917,"tree_line_start":909},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n A disability additional payment is made to each individual who is entitled to a payment of a \ndisability benefit.\n ","tree_line_end":925,"tree_line_start":918},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP)Act 22, s 5","tree_line_end":931,"tree_line_start":926},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Qualifying Disability Benefits","tree_line_end":936,"tree_line_start":932},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"10. The list of qualifying benefits includes","tree_line_end":940,"tree_line_start":937},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n1.\n Attendance Allowance","tree_line_end":952,"tree_line_start":941},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n2. \nConstant Attendance Allowance","tree_line_end":964,"tree_line_start":953},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n3.\n Disability Living Allowance for adults","tree_line_end":976,"tree_line_start":965},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n 4.\n Disability Living Allowance for children","tree_line_end":987,"tree_line_start":977},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n5.\n Personal Independence Payment","tree_line_end":999,"tree_line_start":988},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n6.\n Adult disability payment (Scotland)","tree_line_end":1011,"tree_line_start":1000},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n7.\n Child disability payment (Scotland)","tree_line_end":1022,"tree_line_start":1012},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n8.\n Armed Forces independent payment","tree_line_end":1034,"tree_line_start":1023},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n9.\n War pension mobility supplement.","tree_line_end":1046,"tree_line_start":1035},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note: \nThe full list of qualifying disability benefits can be found in the legislation\n1\n.\n \n \n \n ","tree_line_end":1060,"tree_line_start":1047},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (AP)Act 22, s 5(2)","tree_line_end":1066,"tree_line_start":1061},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n ","tree_line_end":1076,"tree_line_start":1067},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"EFFECT ON SOCIAL SECURITY BENEFITS","tree_line_end":1081,"tree_line_start":1077},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"11. No account is to be taken of any cost of living additional payments when considering a person’s \nentitlement to a means tested social security benefit\n1\n.","tree_line_end":1090,"tree_line_start":1082},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n For calculating benefit entitlement purposes the additional payment is completely ignored.","tree_line_end":1096,"tree_line_start":1091},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS(AP) Act 2022, s 8\n ","tree_line_end":1103,"tree_line_start":1097},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"12. Additional cost of living payments\n1\n are an entirely new benefit which are\n \nautomatically passported \nfrom existing benefit entitlement. Therefore, there\n \n ","tree_line_end":1116,"tree_line_start":1104},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n \n \nis no entitlement decision \nand\n ","tree_line_end":1129,"tree_line_start":1117},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n \n \nare no rights of appeal\n ","tree_line_end":1140,"tree_line_start":1130},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"in respect of these payments.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ","tree_line_end":1246,"tree_line_start":1141},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS(AP) Act 22, s 6","tree_line_end":1252,"tree_line_start":1247},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"CONTACTS","tree_line_end":1257,"tree_line_start":1253},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"If you have any queries about this memo, please write to Decision Making and Appeals (DMA) Leeds, 3E \nzone E, Quarry House, Leeds. Existing arrangements for such referrals should be followed, as set out \nin\n \nMemo ADM 7/19\n Requesting case guidance from DMA Leeds for all benefits.","tree_line_end":1269,"tree_line_start":1258},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"DMA Leeds: August 2022","tree_line_end":1275,"tree_line_start":1270},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1279,"tree_line_start":1276},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"The content of the examples in this document (including use of imagery) is for illustrative purposes only","tree_line_end":1283,"tree_line_start":1280}],"bounds":{"stderr_bytes":65536,"stdout_bytes":16777216,"timeout_seconds":45},"command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/pdfinfo","-struct-text","source/adm-2026-09-19/pdf/adm-memo-17-22.pdf"],"diagnostics":{"roles_not_emitted":{"Document":1,"Link":2,"Sect":1,"Span":82},"text_joiner":"\n","tree_lines":1283,"unparsed_line_count":2,"unparsed_line_samples":[{"text":"        Object 439 0","tree_line":471},{"text":"        Object 436 0","tree_line":1268}],"unparsed_line_samples_omitted":0},"document_id":"adm-memo-17-22","document_key":"adm:adm-memo-17-22","family":"adm","frozen_tagged_flag":"yes","limitations":["PDF-declared roles are source structure, not proof of correct reading order, accessibility, coherent legal units or applicability.","Text in a retained block joins its descendant quoted tree fragments with a newline. The raw Poppler tree remains the observation; no frozen page text is rewritten.","Parent and child blocks deliberately overlap. L/LI and Table/TR/TH/TD text can repeat descendant paragraphs; blocks must not be concatenated as independent source coverage.","Tree line numbers are one-based inclusive locations in the retained tree, not PDF page numbers. Matching to immutable page-text offsets is a separate proposal.","Only H1-H6, P, Table, TR, TH, TD, L and LI blocks are emitted. Other roles remain in raw tree text and diag